    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d45">

                <pb facs="0116" n="1184" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v05p2/pg1184"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.5/9–254</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to Foreign Minister Spaak
                        </hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d45-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1954-09-13">September 13,
                        1954</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>I wish to thank you for your message to me of September 3.<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d45-f2"/> As you know, I have for the last several days been absent
                    from Washington and I am sure you understand my pre-occupation with the problems
                    of the Manila Conference.</p>
                <p>I share fully your concern over the gravity of the problems we now face as the
                    result of French rejection of the EDC. We are in process of developing urgently
                    our thinking here on the steps which should be taken next, and receiving your
                    views has been most helpful in this connection. I hope that we will in the very
                    near future be in a position to discuss our views with you. We shall of course
                    want to consult fully with you and your Government well in advance of the
                    forthcoming meeting of the North Atlantic Council.</p>
                <p>I am looking forward in particular to discussing this problem with you personally
                    at the forthcoming meeting of the General Assembly in New York.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dulles</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d45-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d45-f1-content">
                <p>This message was transmitted to Brussels in telegram 301, Sept. 13, with
                    instructions that it be delivered to Spaak.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d45-f2" n="2" xml:id="d45-f2-content">
